Organization = {Univ Teknologi MARA (UiTM), FAPS, Ctr Environm Behav Studies (cE Bs)},
Abstract = {In the current global momentum of Eco and Smart Growth, Green
   Infrastructure (GI) concept is proving a popular means to accomplish
   sustainable development. This study's aim was to develop a Green
   Infrastructure Gauge (GIG), whose goal was to maximize presence of GI
   elements and functions in future urban master plans, and gauge GI status
   in existing urban areas. We derived relative value for each GI function
   through a questionnaire survey to public workers in 41 Japanese
   municipalities. It highlights the most valuable GI elements and
   functions future towns and cities can incorporate, to realize ecosystems
   and environment wellbeing, and herald sustainable future communities.
