Abstract = {At present, most Chinese researches focus on eco-tourism instead of
   eco-leisure, since ecotourism can bring direct economic and
   environmental benefits. In fact, eco-leisure activities, which can be
   engaged in short spare time, connect more closely with people's daily
   life than eco-tourism activities, which must be taken in longer
   holidays. In this paper, the authors firstly review Urban Green Space
   based Eco-leisure (UGSEL) literatures, then, presents a theoretical
   model for studying the UGSEL in China.},
