Note = {4th International Conference on Urban Air Quality, Charles Univ, Prague,
   CZECH REPUBLIC, MAR 25-28, 2003},
Abstract = {OFIS is a robust and efficient model for simulating the formation of
   photochemical pollutants in all urban plume. In this paper we present
   applications of the recent further development of OFIS for calculating
   both particulate matter and ozone concentrations.
   In particular, we refer to the analysis of the model performance in the
   framework of the project MERLIN and the CITYDELTA exercise. OFIS was
   applied to simulate the urban plume Formation of Milan. Berlin and their
   surrounding areas for a period of six months to one year. In this paper
   model results are presented as appropriate indicators of long term
   pollution of ozone and particulate matter and the model performance is
   assessed on the basis of available observational evidence using
   appropriate statistical indices. (c) 2005 Elsevier Ltd. All rights
