   Telecommunication, Broadcasting, and Satellite (TelSaTech), Jakarta,
   INDONESIA, AUG 02-03, 2013},
Abstract = {Participation of young voters considered can contribute a lot in the
   Presidential Election. Therefore, the Electoral Commission in Indonesia
   has encourage the students to be more active in the 2014 Election. Ahead
   of the Presidential Election campaign, many television news programs
   present political issues to attract the voters attention. One of the
   models of political news content is designed in the form of live
   interview with resource persons. The live interview can be a means to
   construct the audience's perception of political issues, particularly
   through the role of news anchor and resource persons as visual elements
   or participants. Qualitative method with semiotic approach is used to
   analyze the visual elements on the live interview as television show.
   The quantitative results shows the half of students have the perception
   that resource persons did not represent the interests of the people and
   untrustworthy.},
