   Modeling with the International Congress on Environmental Modelling and
   Software (iEMSs), Ottawa, CANADA, JUL 05-08, 2010},
Abstract = {This emergy-based four angle model application is used to depict the
   variations of urban metabolic profile (energy and money) based on the
   changes experienced across the economic sectors over the years. The
   urban metabolic structure and efficiency results obtained for Beijing
   are compared to those for other European cities. In addition, for the
   Beijing's case, the study creates the foundation for a future analysis
   comparing the development of Beijing with that of Rome. The results
   imply that over three decade Beijing's urbanizing movement has greatly
   promoted the sustained development of the real estate and growth of
   urban household. The results also indicate that the emergy-based four
   angle model can be refined to become an integrative tool for evaluation,
   policy-making and regulation for ecosystem management concerning
   structure and efficiency at urban levels. (c) 2011 Published by Elsevier
   Ltd.},
