Abstract = {The automatic detection and study of human emotions has always been an
   area of interest within the scientific community. The AUBADE European
   Union funded project has addressed this problem by developing an
   innovative, intelligent, multi-sensor and wearable system for the
   assessment of the emotional state of humans under special conditions
   (i.e. neurological diseases, stress, etc.). The system recognizes the
   emotions after processing biomedical signals ( electromyogram,
   electrocardiogram, respiration rate and galvanic skin response) and can
   be applied in diverse areas. Currently, a health care sector scenario
   has been considered and validated, primarily in the neurology and
   psychology areas, in order to contribute to get precise diagnosis and
