   CORPORATE SOCIAL RESPONSIBILITY: TOURISM, MICE AND MANAGEMENT TECHNIQUE
   SESSION},
Year = {2008},
Pages = {53-57},
Note = {Euro-Asia Conference on Environment and Corporate Social Responsibility
   - Tourism, MICE and Management Technique Session, Tianjin, PEOPLES R
   CHINA, JAN 18-19, 2008},
Abstract = {In this paper, the author attempts to find out the traveling motives of
   Chinese urban residents based on an empirical study conducted in Zi Bo,
   which located in the Shandong province in east China. She divides
   tourists into three categories according to their travel motives, i.e.
   tourists seeking fresh experiences,. tourists retrieving
   good-old-experiences, and tourists without clear motives. The research
   shows that travel motives of most Chinese urban residents tend to be
   fresh experiences seeking. Although only few urban residents travel
   without clear motives, the potential market for such tourists seems to
   be very attractive with the fast increase of the group. This research
   may contribute to facilitate the development of Chinese tourism
   destinations through strategy management.},
