Note = {World Conference on Psychology, Counselling and Guidance (WCPCG 2010),
   Antalya, TURKEY, APR 22-25, 2010},
Abstract = {The Brief Illness Perception Questionnaire (Brief IPQ) provides a rapid
   assessment of illness perception. This study investigated reliability
   and validity of a Farsi version of the Brief Illness Perception
   Questionnaire (Brief IPQ). 300 patients with type I diabetes (128 males
   and 172 females) from Iranian Diabetes Society were asked to complete
   the Brief Illness Perception Questionnaire (Brief IPQ), and
   Psychological Well-being subscale of Mental Health Inventory (MHI).
   Also, HbA(1c) was obtained from laboratory examination. The results
   revealed good internal consistency, construct validity, and concurrent
   validity with other measures. The results showed that the scale has
   cross-cultural validity. (C) 2010 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.},
