Note = {3rd World Conference on Psychology, Counselling and Guidance (WCPCG),
   Efes, TURKEY, MAY 09-12, 2012},
Abstract = {The aim of the study was to explore how eating disordered (ED) patients
   perceive their illness and to investigate the relation between illness
   representation and motivation to recover. 45 eating disordered females
   took part in the study. They were asked to complete the Eating Attitudes
   Test (EAT-26), a questionnaire for motivation assessment (ANSOCQ or
   BNSOCQ) and Brief-Illness Perception Questionnaire (B-IPQ). Qualitative
   data about personally significant aspects were included. Results
   revealed that participants view the illness as short lasting and not a
   severe disorder. The study confirmed the relation between subjective
   illness perception and motivation to recover. (C) 2013 The Authors.
