   Responsibility - Tourism, Society and Education Session, Berlin,
   GERMANY, AUG 29-30, 2014},
Organization = {Tianjin Univ Finance \& Econ, Tourism Dept; IMRE Alumni Network; German
   Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; TU Bergakademie Freiberg},
Abstract = {Based on researches of a traditional Tibetan Abhay village in the
   Nyingchi district, the author finds out that Tibetans have strong
   perception on economic impacts of sustainable tourism development;
   however, the perception on social-cultural and environmental impacts of
   tourism development is relatively weak. In order to gain more economic
   benefits, most local people take appropriate actions in promoting
   tourism development, such as building family hotels, seeking for funds,
   starting to negotiation, learning Chinese and protecting Tibetan
   culture, etc. Thus, it is necessary to provide development assistance in
   guiding the positive perception of local residents on social and
   environmental impacts of sustainable tourism development and encourage
   them to engage in sustainable tourism development.},
