   Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; Germany Embassy Thailand; Thai Govt},
Abstract = {Urban mass transit system can be regarded as public goods. At present,
   management of Chinese urban mass transit is lack of public participation
   due to the governmental-dominating administration mechanism. This
   implies that NGOs cannot play important roles in influencing public
   decision making in terms of urban mass transit projects with long life
   span. In this paper, the authors initiate a new concept, i.e. Virtual
   NGOs, with comparative advantages than the existing NGOs. Then, they
   further discuss a model which facilitates sustainable development of
   urban mass transit system through public participation based on Virtual
   NGOs.},
