Note = {22nd Congress of the International Ergonomics Association-IEA, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {Literature suggests focusing on the built environment for designing
   healthy and inclusive neighbourhoods by applying the urban health
   approach. However, it is still difficult to address these issues through
   an urban product design perspective and an inclusive lens. This paper
   aims to clarify this aspect starting from the data provided with an
   action research project aimed at finding scenarios for healthy and
   inclusive neighbourhoods. Specifically, from this project best practices
   were extracted and analysed for understanding how to assume an inclusive
   perspective to design healthy and inclusive neighbourhoods. As a result,
   the study proposes categories divided into design instruments, best
   practices, and urban products that may help in designing healthy and
   inclusive neighbourhoods from a micro-level perspective. Finally, the
   paper discusses these categories as a toolbox for the positionality
   toward inclusion of designers, policy-makers and citizens.},
