   landscape quality:: Konya case},
Booktitle = {XXX IAHS WORLD CONGRESS ON HOUSING, HOUSING CONSTRUCTION: AN
   INTERDISCIPLINARY TASK, VOLS 1-3},
Year = {2002},
Pages = {1067-1073},
Note = {30th IAHS World Congress on Housing, UNIV COIMBRA, COIMBRA, PORTUGAL,
   SEP 09-13, 2002},
Organization = {Int Assoc Housing Sci},
Abstract = {Konya as being one of the oldest settlements of Anatolia inhabited by
   many civilisations has a splendid historical past as far as human
   habitats are concerned. The city is located at Central Anatolian Region
   developed on a plain land called Konya Plateau having the oldest
   settlements in its borders till prehistoric times. Konya as being the
   capital of Se1jukid Era, exhibits on one hand the character of a
   Se1jukid settlement and the traces of Turkish culture with its unique
   pattern, monumental buildings and the traditional houses and carries the
   traces of the Hittite housing culture on the other hand. However, the
   settlement is changing rapidly day by day by the addition of numerous
   contemporary buildings and housing areas in an unhealthy urban
   development.
   In this paper, housing design, housing areas and their relation with the
   environment will be discussed for Konya City in case of urban
   development and landscaping. There are mainly three dominant types of
   housing areas in the urban development of Konya city exhibiting
   different housing character, urban pattern and landscape qualities.
   Villa type of housing areas with 2-3 storeys in low density tissues
   having large gardens, mass housing areas formed of multi-storey huge
   blocks in a compact manner developed in various parts of the city as
   extensions of the urban tissue and the traditional flat roofed old
   housing areas integrated to the main/old city center constructed with
   adobe are the main three types of housing developments in Konya. Urban
   design approaches, landscaping and it's quality was criticised for these
   areas spanned to the data obtained from urban and housing
   studies/researches made for Konya. Three different types of housing
   areas dominant in Konya was evaluated and a comparative discussion in
   case of urban planning, landscape design and environmental quality for
   various housing areas was made and these housing models and their
   contribution and/or effects to the urban environment was discussed.},
