Note = {17th Urban Data Management Symposium (UDMS 94), HELSINKI ESPOO, FINLAND,
   SEP 04-08, 1994},
Abstract = {An integrated approach to the development of a computer system for urban
   facilities maintenance is proposed. In this paper rye consider every-day
   operations and alarm management for gas-, heat-, water-supply and sewage
   urban networks. Growth of towns results in the necessity for
   computer-aided processing of the geographical and attributive
   information, facilities networks simulations and simulation results
   analysis, real-time process monitoring. These tasks are suggested as the
   main ones for urban computer systems We present our point of view on
   each of these tasks separately and discuss various scenarios of the
   tasks using results. As a result of discussion the structure of
   complicated computer system combining GIS, SCADA, CAD and DBMS features
   is proposed The variant of a PC-based system which applies the
   principles of integration is described The ideas and software and
   hardware features. we suggest, are of interest to both engineers and
   managers in the urban facilities domain.},
