Organization = {IACSIT; Environm Sci Soc},
Abstract = {The rural livelihood system in Zambia is essentially agricultural, and
   agriculture is the main link between people and their environment.
   Through agricultural activities people seek to husband the available
   soil, water and biological resources so as to ``harvest{''} a livelihood
   for themselves. Poor people, especially those living in marginal
   environments and areas with low agricultural productivity in Zambia,
   depend directly on genetic, species and ecosystem diversity to support
   their way of life. As a result of this dependency, any impact that
   climate change has on natural systems will threaten the livelihoods,
   intake and health of the population. This, study was aimed at assessing
   Risk perceptions and Attitude of climate change by peasant farmers in
   Zambia using Affective Imagery and Decision making analysis. The sample
   had a relatively strong negative affect associated with global warming.
   The results indicate that greater perception of the severity of climate
   change problems cause respondents to be more aware of the degradation of
   the environment. The more individuals are aware of the existence of the
   degradation of the environment and of its consequences, the more likely
   they are to do something about it in order to ameliorate the situation},
