Note = {4th International Symposium on Highway Pollution, MADRID, SPAIN, MAY
   18-22, 1992},
Abstract = {To observe the required quality in Danish receiving water systems,
   pollution from urban and highway run-off is of importance in many cases.
   There is therefore a potential demand for treatment of the wet-weather
   flow. An evaluation of relevant treatment methods was carried out for
   the National Agency for Environmental Protection. The wet detention pond
   was considered the most efficient and suitable solution for removal of
   the most important pollutants, i.e. phosphorus and heavy metals, in the
   storm-water run-off from urban catchments and highways. Recommended
   design procedures are described and exemplified in this paper.},
