Organization = {German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {Studies on the residents' perceptions and attitudes toward tourism
   destinations attract increasingly more attention. Along with the rapid
   tourism development, some tourist residents have not only failed to get
   real benefits, but even face threat to lose their own interests.
   Consequently, they are disgusted with the development of tourism if this
   kind of phenomenon continues. In order to promote sustained and healthy
   development of tourism, it is necessary to study the perception and
   attitudes of local residents in scenic spots. In the paper, the
   residents' perceptions and attitudes in the Lingyan temple religion
   scenic spot was investigated. Study of the authors show that local
   resident in the Lingyan temple religion scenic spot have been strongly
   discontented to the economic profit. Most of local residents were
   dissatisfied for the uneven distribution and more satisfied the
   environmental impact. There were significant differences in the
   perception of local residents with different income levels, different
   space distance and different belief. The benefits of community residents
   have close relationships with the sustainable development of religion
   tourism. When the community residents take an active part in tourism
   development and benefit from it, the community harmony and the
   sustainable development of the religion tourism can be realized.},
