   15-17, 2008},
Abstract = {Laser range finder has been widely used as an accurate external sensor
   for mobile robots. A key issue for building accurate and robust
   perception model for laser range finder is how to detect and filter out
   the invalid measurements. The paper presents a method to detect and to
   filter out invalid beams of laser range finder, and based on this,
   constructs a robust perception model for it. The robustness for the
   perception model was two folds: firstly, two features are extracted to
   detect invalid beams; secondly, the beams occluded by dynamical objects
   are also picked out. The presented perception model is testified in
   localization for mobile robots.},
