   Cooperat Eco Urban Design; Sichuan Univ; Shanghai Univ Electric Power;
   BEEUE; Int Clean Energy Talent Program; UNiLAB},
Abstract = {As energy, environmental and climate issues have become increasingly
   prominent, it has been widely agreed that the development of clean
   energy represented by solar energy, wind energy, and geothermal energy
   will be vigorously promoted. As an effective carrier for coordinated
   conversion and coordinated and efficient operation among different
   energy quality and diversified energy varieties, the integrated energy
   system is gaining more and more attention and policy support. In this
   paper, according to the heating and power supply requirements of the
   park-type integrated energy system during the heating period, a
   mixed-integer model for optimal scheduling of the system is proposed.
   The model chooses two types of economic and environmental goals, and
   comprehensively considers the balance between supply and demand of the
   hourly load and the operational characteristics of each energy supply
   device. Especially, the model takes into account the water distribution
   rules of the heating supply system. Finally, a typical day is selected
   to verify the effectiveness of the proposed model. The result shows
   that, compared to its environmental operation, the system's economic
   operation has 18.7\% of cost saving while has a 3.4\% of more energy
   consumption. Copyright 2018 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.},
