   Technologies and Infrastructure to Enhance Urban Ecosystem Services
   (SSC), RUDN Univ, Moscow, RUSSIA, MAY 23-26, 2018},
Organization = {RUDN Univ Program 5-100; Erasmus+ Jean Monnet Project European Tradit
   Governance Design \& Environm Management Megacities Search Solut},
Abstract = {Noise-proof properties of green spaces are studied on the streets with
   heavy road traffic in Saint-Petersburg. Noise reduction is considered
   depending on the species composition and planning concept of the
   plantings. It has been shown that planning concepts such as number of
   rows or widths of tree planting are more important for noise reduction
   than species composition of trees and shrubs. The double-row planting of
   deciduous trees with a green band width of more than 18 m and crowns
   overlapping of neighboring trees by 60-70\% has the best noise
   protection features.},
